# Link-check exclusions for the docs "Link Check" job (.github/workflows/docs.yml).
#
# Each line is a regex matched against the URL. Keep this list short and keep
# every entry justified -- an exclusion is a link nobody is checking. Verified
# against lychee 0.24: with this file the check reports 0 errors, and without
# it exactly the entry below fails.

# npmjs.com answers 403 to any client without a browser user agent, whether or
# not the package exists, so checking it only ever produces a false positive.
# The npm version badge beside this link is served by shields.io and is checked.
^https://www\.npmjs\.com/package/

# Not listed here on purpose:
#   - Schema URLs in example code blocks are not requested without
#     --include-verbatim. Published v1 URLs belong to hushspec.org; historical
#     v0 identifiers retain hushspec.dev but use the documented .org mirror.
#   - https://crates.io/crates/hushspec resolves today; leave it checked so the
#     link breaks loudly if the crate is ever unpublished or renamed.
